  f you create a framework

Suppose you invent your own framework called TravelChain.

You would follow essentially the same process:

1. Create TravelChain folder
2. Write Python modules
3. Test locally
4. git init
5. Create GitHub repository
6. Push the code
7. Add an open-source licence (for example, MIT)
8. Write a README
9. Publish to PyPI
10. Share it with the developer community
11. Review pull requests from contributors
12. Continue releasing improved versions

That is the standard lifecycle followed by many successful open-source projects, including LangChain.

